A||||7||JohnnyK||Testing for alcohol content||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||09-02-2001||02:37 PM||||Me and my buddies have started making our own beer (well, we have for a while) but I want to know what the alcohol content is in it. Any way to test? (Don't give me some crap like "Freeze it and see how much turns to ice" or something like that..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||09-02-2001||02:40 PM||||Specific gravity! Use a hydrometer...<P>OOOOooor, you could drink 10 reg'lar beers, note effects, then drink 10 of yours and compare results. Don't try this with Scumble.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||09-02-2001||02:45 PM||||I dont know how they do it in breweies, but freezing it and carefully measureing the temp at which it freezes, or thaws or something like that would be one way.<P> alcohol alters the freezing point of water - the more thats in there, the more its altered - I have no idea how its done professionally though<P>  another way, there is probabally something like a hydrometer you float in the beer, same as you use to check your antifreeze.<P>  or maybe you have to send it to a lab.<P>  The best way is to see how many pints you have to drink before you pass out, then see how many pints of Coors you have to drink before you pass out, then the alcohol content of your beer will be a ratio<P>  Pints of yours / pints of Coors = % in Coors / % in yours<P>  [its an inversly proportional ratio cause the higher the % of alcohol, the fewer pints it takes.<P>  If you want me to run this test for you send about 4 cases and Ill let you know :c)||||reg||10
Z||000003||JohnnyK||09-02-2001||03:03 PM||||Trust me, you DON'T want to drink our beer..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> But anyways, my drinking/passingout/puking ratio differs from day to day. IE, i can drink 12 beers one day and be fine, but the next day, I can only have 6... soooo, twould not be a very specific test.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||09-02-2001||03:04 PM||||Just draw a glass, and use a battery hyrometer. DON'T DRINK IT!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000005||Wolfhound||09-02-2001||07:36 PM||||You can find an inexpensive hydrometer at any brewery supply that already calibrated for alcohol content. Check around on the net.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||09-03-2001||02:57 AM||||Try lighting it with a match, if the match goes out, not enough alcohol.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierohoho||09-03-2001||03:46 AM||||JohnnyK, I would check the web for a site on homebrewing. <P>Maybe even a forum for it. <P>I would think you could get in touch with someone that way who could give you a rough guess by how you brewed the beer. <P>Or send it to an independant lab for testing $$$$$$$. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
